90
00:03:27,790 --> 00:03:31,149
But we don't want to spend too long on that.

91
00:03:31,149 --> 00:03:34,507
The other students will already know a bit about it.

92
00:03:34,507 --> 00:03:37,530
It's all to do with communications and so on.

93
00:03:37,530 --> 00:03:38,029
CARLA:

94
00:03:38,029 --> 00:03:38,528
Yes.

95
00:03:38,528 --> 00:03:46,009
We should mention some geographical factors, things like wetlands and river estuaries and coastal erosion

96
00:03:46,009 --> 00:03:47,505
and so on.

97
00:03:47,505 --> 00:03:53,490
We could have some maps of different cities with these features marked.

98
00:03:53,490 --> 00:03:53,957
ROB:

99
00:03:53,957 --> 00:03:56,290
On a handout you mean?

100
00:03:56,290 --> 00:03:59,090
Or some slides everyone can see?

101
00:03:59,090 --> 00:03:59,788
CARLA:

102
00:03:59,788 --> 00:04:00,486
Yeah,

103
00:04:00,486 --> 00:04:02,580
