108
00:04:13,670 --> 00:04:14,022
CARLA:

109
00:04:14,022 --> 00:04:14,375
Yes.

110
00:04:14,375 --> 00:04:18,954
We could use that as the basis for that part of the talk.

111
00:04:18,954 --> 00:04:22,477
I don't think the other students will have read it,

112
00:04:22,477 --> 00:04:26,000
but they'll remember hearing about the flooding at the time.

113
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:26,857
ROB:

114
00:04:26,857 --> 00:04:27,714
OK.

115
00:04:27,714 --> 00:04:32,000
So that's probably enough background.

116
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:32,392
CARLA:

117
00:04:32,392 --> 00:04:37,886
So then we'll go on to talk about what action's being taken to deal

118
00:04:37,886 --> 00:04:40,240
with the problems of coastal cities.

119
00:04:40,240 --> 00:04:40,667
ROB:

120
00:04:40,667 --> 00:04:41,093
OK.

121
00:04:41,093 --> 00:04:44,505
What else do we need to talk about?

122
00:04:44,505 --> 00:04:50,477
Maybe something on future risks, looking more at the long term, if populations continue

123
00:04:50,477 --> 00:04:51,330
